MAYOR OF SURAKARTA

CENTRAL JAVA PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF THE CITY OF SURAKARTA NUMBER 7 OF 2024

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD THE MAYOR OF SURAKARTA,

COPY

Considering : a. that women are citizens who have human rights that must be protected, respected, upheld, and may not be neglected, reduced, or deprived by anyone, and therefore need to receive protection from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;

b. that in order to realize the fulfillment of women's constitutional rights to be free from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination, and to improve the quality of life of women, they need to receive protection and empowerment from the Regional Government;

c. that the implementation of the protection of women in the Region has not been able to be carried out optimally and is accompanied by the continued occurrence of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women, so that comprehensive regulation is needed to provide direction, foundation, and legal certainty;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 16 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Large City Regions within the Province of East Java, Central Java, West Java and the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 45);

3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as most recently amended several times by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);

4. Law Number 12 of 2022 concerning the Criminal Act of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6792);

5. Law Number 11 of 2023 concerning Central Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 58 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6867);

With Joint Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF THE CITY OF SURAKARTA and

MAYOR OF SURAKARTA

HAS DECIDED:

To Enact : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN.

Article 10

(1) Services implemented to fulfill the rights of women victims shall be carried out with the following principles:

a. respect for human rights; b. non-discrimination;
c. confidentiality;
d. empathy;
e. inclusion;
f. empowerment;
g. victim-based decisions;
h. honesty;
i. professionalism;
j. integration; and
k. sustainability.
(2) The provision of services to victims shall be carried out in an integrated manner by UPTD PPA.
(3) In the provision of services as referred to in paragraph (1), UPTD PPA may cooperate with:
a. community health centers, hospitals, and other health service facilities;
b. technical implementing units handling affairs in the field of social affairs;
c. detention centers, correctional institutions, and correctional centers;
d. police;
e. prosecution;
f. courts;
g. technical implementing units of agencies that provide protection for migrant workers; h. provincial regional offices of ministries that administer government affairs in the field of religion;
i. regional offices and technical implementing units of Ministries that administer government affairs in the field of law and human rights;
j. regional representatives of the Witness and Victim Protection Agency;
k. social welfare implementing institutions; l. community-based service provider institutions; and
m. other institutions.

Article 4

(1) Every woman has the right:

a. to life;
b. to have a family and continue offspring; c. to self-development;
d. to obtain justice;
e. to personal freedom;
f. to security;
g. to welfare; and
h. to participate in government.
(2) The right to life as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a includes:
a. the right to sustain life and improve the standard of living;
b. the right to obtain peace of mind, sense of security, sense of peace, happiness, physical and spiritual welfare; and
c. the right to a good and healthy environment. (3) The right to have a family and continue offspring as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, namely the right to form a family and continue offspring through lawful marriage in accordance with religion and the provisions of laws and regulations. (4) The right to self-development as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c, includes:
a. the right to fulfillment of basic needs to grow and develop properly;
b. the right to protection for personal development, to obtain education, enlighten oneself and improve quality of life in order to become a human being who is faithful, pious, responsible, of noble character, happy, and prosperous in accordance with human rights;
c. the right to develop and obtain benefits from science and technology, arts and culture in accordance with human dignity for the welfare of oneself, nation, and humanity;
d. the right to communicate and obtain information necessary to develop oneself and social environment in accordance with religious, social, and legal norms;
e. the right to seek, obtain, own, store, process, and convey information using all types of available means in accordance with religious, social, and legal norms;
f. the right to fight for the right to self-development, both individually and collectively, to build society, nation, and country in accordance with religious, social, and legal norms;
g. the right to perform social work in accordance with religious, social, and legal norms;
h. the right to participate in the planning and implementation of government policies in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
