k. trade;
l. youth and sports;
m. politics;
n. public tranquility, order, and protection of the Community;
o. public works and spatial planning;
p. public housing and settlement areas; q. women empowerment and child protection; r. population administration and civil registration; s. population control and family planning; and
t. other related fields.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan coordinated by the Regional Apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of Protection and Empowerment of Women.

Article 7

The implementation of the Protection of Women includes efforts to:

a. prevent and protect women from acts of violence, exploitation, and discrimination in a fast, integrated, and coordinated manner;
b. provide services to victims of violence, exploitation and discrimination;
c. empower women;
d. fulfill the special needs of women; and e. improve family quality.

Article 6

(1) The forms of Violence referred to in Article 5 include:

a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. economic violence;
e. exploitation; and
f. KBGO.
(2) Economic Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d includes:
a. taking full control over the victim's income, including salary, savings, or other financial assistance received by the victim:
b. restricting or prohibiting the victim from having or using money, so that the victim is completely dependent on the perpetrator for financial needs:
c. prohibiting or preventing the victim from working or continuing education with the purpose of limiting the victim's financial independence:
d. using the victim's assets or property for personal gain or damaging such assets as a form of punishment; and
e. making all financial decisions without involving the victim, so that the victim has no control over household finances.
(3) Exploitation as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e at a minimum:
a. exploiting women's labor by providing inadequate wages, forcing excessive working hours, or not providing safe and healthy working conditions;
b. exploiting women for sexual purposes, through coercion, deception, or pressure. Including human trafficking for prostitution or pornography production; and
c. exploiting women unfairly in economic transactions, such as providing loans with very high interest or manipulating the market for personal gain.
(4) KBGO as referred to in paragraph (1) letter f, includes:
a. comments or messages that are insulting, degrading, or belittling women;
b. messages or comments that threaten to commit physical or sexual violence against women;
c. disseminating the victim's personal information (such as address, phone number, or other identity) without permission with the purpose of intimidating or harming the victim;
d. extortion involving threats to spread intimate images or videos of the victim unless the victim meets the perpetrator's demands;
e. spreading private photos or videos of an intimate nature without the consent of the women in the content;
f. the use of technology to stalk or continuously monitor the victim, often with the purpose of frightening or controlling the victim; and
g. digitally altering images or videos of women for the purpose of insulting, humiliating, or sexually exploiting.

MAYOR OF SURAKARTA

MAYOR OF SURAKARTA

CENTRAL JAVA PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF THE CITY OF SURAKARTA NUMBER 7 OF 2024

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD THE MAYOR OF SURAKARTA,

COPY

Considering : a. that women are citizens who have human rights that must be protected, respected, upheld, and may not be neglected, reduced, or deprived by anyone, and therefore need to receive protection from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;

b. that in order to realize the fulfillment of women's constitutional rights to be free from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination, and to improve the quality of life of women, they need to receive protection and empowerment from the Regional Government;

c. that the implementation of the protection of women in the Region has not been able to be carried out optimally and is accompanied by the continued occurrence of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women, so that comprehensive regulation is needed to provide direction, foundation, and legal certainty;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 16 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Large City Regions within the Province of East Java, Central Java, West Java and the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 45);

3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as most recently amended several times by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);

4. Law Number 12 of 2022 concerning the Criminal Act of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6792);

5. Law Number 11 of 2023 concerning Central Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 58 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6867);

With Joint Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF THE CITY OF SURAKARTA and

MAYOR OF SURAKARTA

HAS DECIDED:

To Enact : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN.

